{"recall":{"defs":[["Attribute","A property of an object; a.k.a. feature, variable, field."],["Outlier","An object very different from most others; may be noise or the target."],["Imputation","Filling missing values with estimates."],["Stratified sampling","Sampling that preserves group proportions."],["Normalisation","Rescaling to a fixed range (min-max)."],["Standardisation","Centring and scaling to unit variance (z-score)."]],"formulas":["\\text{IQR}=Q_3-Q_1,\\ \\ [Q_1-1.5\\,\\text{IQR},\\ Q_3+1.5\\,\\text{IQR}]","[\\mu-3\\sigma,\\ \\mu+3\\sigma]","v'=\\frac{v-\\min_A}{\\max_A-\\min_A}","v'=\\frac{v-\\mu_A}{\\sigma_A}","v'=v/10^j","W=(B-A)/N"],"takeaways":["Identify attribute and data types first; they decide valid operations and encodings.","Quality problems: noise, outliers, wrong/fake values, missing values, duplicates.","Use IQR (robust) or 3-sigma (normal data) for univariate outliers, and investigate before removing.","Split into representative, stratified sets; rebalance only the training data.","Fit scaling and encoding on training data only; engineer features by extraction, selection, construction and transformation."],"confused":[["Normalisation vs standardisation","Fixed range vs zero mean and unit variance."],["Noise vs outlier","Random distortion vs unusual object."],["Interval vs ratio","Arbitrary zero vs true zero."],["Feature extraction vs selection","New combined features vs a subset of existing ones."],["Label vs one-hot encoding","Integers (order implied) vs binary columns."]],"minute":"Preprocessing prepares raw data for learning. Start with attribute types (nominal, ordinal, interval, ratio; discrete or continuous) and data types. Check quality: noise, outliers, wrong or fake values, missing values and duplicates. Aggregate with split–apply–combine, clean inconsistencies, and impute gaps with an appropriate method. Detect outliers with Q1 − 1.5·IQR / Q3 + 1.5·IQR or μ ± 3σ. Split data into representative, stratified sets and rebalance rare classes in training only. Scale with min-max or z-scores fitted on training data, then engineer features through extraction, selection, construction, binning and encoding."},"flashcards":[["Four attribute types","Nominal, ordinal, interval, ratio"],["Discrete vs continuous","Countable values vs real values"],["Data characteristics","Dimensionality, sparsity, resolution, size"],["Six data quality dimensions","Correct, complete, consistent, trustworthy, interpretable, usable on demand"],["Two cases of outliers","Noise to remove, or the target (fraud, intrusion)"],["Imputation options","Zero, last known, mean, interpolation (splines), insert missing records"],["IQR fences","Q1 − 1.5·IQR and Q3 + 1.5·IQR"],["3-sigma fences","μ ± 3σ; ~99.7% of normal data inside"],["Min-max formula","$v'=\\frac{v-\\min}{\\max-\\min}(\\text{new}_{\\max}-\\text{new}_{\\min})+\\text{new}_{\\min}$"],["Z-score","$v'=(v-\\mu)/\\sigma$"],["Decimal scaling","$v'=v/10^j$, smallest j with max|v'| < 1"],["Sampling types","Random, stratified, clustered"],["Feature engineering parts","Extraction, selection, construction, transformation"],["Equal-width bin size","W = (B − A)/N"],["One-hot vs label encoding","Binary column per category vs integer codes (implies order)"]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["why"],"deep":["p-components"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h1","h2"],"deep":["p-data"],"viz":["attrSorter"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3","example"],"deep":["p-types"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["p-quality"],"viz":["outlierLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["what"],"deep":["p-overview"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h5"],"deep":["p-agg"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h6"],"deep":["p-clean"],"viz":["imputeLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7","demo"],"deep":["p-outliers"],"viz":["outlierLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h8"],"deep":["p-sampling"],"viz":["samplingLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h9"],"deep":["p-scali